# One ignore file for both images, because both are built from the repository
# root:
#
#   docker build -t gamematch-api:latest -f apps/server/Dockerfile .
#   docker build -t gamematch-web:latest -f apps/web/Dockerfile .
#
# This is not a substitute for narrow COPY paths — both Dockerfiles copy only
# what they need — but it is the difference between a context of a few hundred
# kilobytes and one carrying .git, node_modules and the demo database.

# Version control: ~9 MB here and never useful inside an image.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Dependencies. The Go module cache is rebuilt by `go mod download` inside the
# build stage; Node and pnpm enter neither image.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Local state: the demo database, its WAL sidecars and uploads, the backup
# directory the compose stack writes to, and the ~19 MB of build output a local
# `go build -o bin/…` leaves in apps/server/bin. That last one matters beyond
# context size: COPY apps/server/ ./ copies the whole directory, so an excluded
# bin/ is what keeps it from invalidating that layer on every local rebuild.
apps/server/data
apps/server/bin
data
backups
.caddytest

# Secrets, at any depth. A bare `.env` pattern is root-anchored in this file
# format, so apps/server/.env and apps/web/.env would match neither it nor
# `.env.*` — and COPY apps/server/ ./ would put one in the build stage. It still
# would not reach the final image (only /out/gamematch is copied), but it would
# land in BuildKit's content store.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Noise, at any depth.
**/*.log

# Not in any image, and large.
docs
.superpowers
.claude
.crush

# apps/web/dist is deliberately NOT excluded: it is the web image's only build
# input, and excluding it makes `docker build -f apps/web/Dockerfile .` fail with
# "not found". It is 624 KB of content-hashed assets.